* Europeana Data Model (EDM) Template for use with University of Chicago Library Digital Collections

* Triple Types
All triples should be typed. Choose from among these types.

#+BEGIN_SRC
a ore:ResourceMap
a ore:Aggregation
a edm:ProvidedCHO
a ore:Proxy # optional
a edm:WebResource
a rdfs:Resource # This is the default type. Use it when
                  none of the preceding apply.
#+END_SRC

Of the above, the ore:Resource Map and ore:Proxy are optional.

* Required Elements
In this section, mandatory Europeana elements are indicated by *boldface*. Mandatory Europeana elements governed by either/or or if/then statements are indicated by /italics/. Mandatory elements required by local usage are _underlined_.

The following is with reference to [[https://pro.europeana.eu/files/Europeana_Professional/Share_your_data/Technical_requirements/EDM_Documentation//EDM_Definition_v5.2.8_102017.pdf][Definition of the Europeana Data Model v5.2.8 06/10/2017]] and the [[https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EF/pages/987791389/EDM+-+Mapping+guidelines][EDM Mapping Guidelines]].

** ore:ResourceMap

The following are required for an ore:ResourceMap, which is optional. The requirements are indicated by example.

#+BEGIN_SRC
<b20x2w73r321/rem>
dcterms:creator "https://node.uchicago.edu/" ;
dcterms:created "2022-02-09T11:21:52-06:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
dcterms:modified "2022-02-09T11:21:52-06:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
ore:describes <b20x2w73r321/aggregation> ;
a ore:ResourceMap .
#+END_SRC

Note that when an ore:ResourceMap is being created, the values of dcterms:created and dcterms:modified are the same.

** ore:Aggregation

The following are mandatory Europeana elements for the ore:Aggregation.

+ Either /edm:isShownAt/ "The URL of a web view of the object in full information context. If there is no edm:isShownAt for an object, there must be a edm:isShownBy. If both are available, provide both. The use of edm:isShownBy is preferred." ([[https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EF/pages/2106032160/ore+Aggregation#edm%3AisShownAt][EDM Mapping Guidelines]]) The example given in the EDM documentation is <edm:isShownAt rdf:resource="http://www.mimo-­‐db.eu/UEDIN/214"/>. This is clearly a website.
+ /edm:isShownBy/ "The URL of a web view of the object. An edm:isShownBy must be provided. If there is no edm:isShownBy for an object, there must be a edm:isShownAt. The use of edm:isShownBy is preferred." ([[https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EF/pages/2106032160/ore+Aggregation#edm%3AisShownBy][EDM Mapping Guidelines]]) The example given in the EDM documentation is <edm:isShownBy rdf:resource="http://www.mimo‐db.eu/media/UEDIN/IMAGE/0032195c.jpg"/>. This is clearly something of a type which we might provide out of the Library Digital Repository via IIIF, e.g., edm:isShownBy <b20b66b16m9w/file.pdf>.

+ *edm:rights*

By convention, we indicate edm:isShownAt by the URL of the mapping ARK identifier (for this terminology, see [[https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-kunze-ark-28#name-ark-anatomy][https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-kunze-ark-28#name-ark-anatomy]]), and edm:isShownBy by appending ``/file.tif'', ``/file.wav'', etc. to the mapping ARK identifier if the file is going to be retrieved from the OCFL disk hierarchy; otherwise, it should have its own mapping ARK identifier, e.g., if it is going to be served by an external system such as Panopto. 

Local usage specifies the following:

: uchicago:inCollection <http://lib.uchicago.edu/uchicagonode>

In addition to uchicago:inCollection =<http://lib.uchicago.edu/uchicagonode>=, which local usage requires for the edm:ProvidedCHO, one or more additional uchicago:inCollection predicates should be specified, for example, =<http://lib.uchicago.edu/chopin-early-editions>= in the case of Chopin Early Editions.

The following is an example of an ore:Aggregation. The order is specified by [[https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/x/IICHfQ][Europeana's documentation]].

#+BEGIN_SRC
<b20x2w73r321/aggregation>                                                                                                            
edm:aggregatedCHO <b20x2w73r321> ;                                                                                                    
edm:dataProvider "University of Chicago Library" ;                                                                                    
edm:isShownAt <b20x2w73r321> ;                                                                                                        
edm:isShownBy <b20x2w73r321/file.wav> ;                                                                                               
edm:object "https://www.lib.uchicago.edu/dl/images/audio.jpg" ;[1]                                                                        
edm:provider "University of Chicago Library" ;                                                                                        
edm:rights "https://rightsstatements.org/vocab/NoC-US/1.0/" ;[2]                                                                      
uchicago:inCollection <lib.uchicago.edu/uchicagonode>, <lib.uchicago.edu/mesoamerican-languages-collection>, <lib.uchicago.edu/online-language-archive> ;                                       
ore:isDescribedBy <b9m865s34c01/rem> ;                                                                                                
a ore:Aggregation .
#+END_SRC

See also [[https://github.com/uchicago-library/UChicagoNode/wiki/Notes][https://github.com/uchicago-library/UChicagoNode/wiki/Notes]] for collections which may belong to more than one collection other than <lib.uchicago.edu/uchicagonode>.

The ore:Aggregation may contain edm:hasView (the value is a link to edm:WebResource). See [[https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EF/pages/2106032160/ore+Aggregation#edm%3AhasView][https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EF/pages/2106032160/ore+Aggregation#edm%3AhasView]] for usage.

[1] The URL of a representation of the CHO which will be used for generating previews for use in the Europeana portal.
This may be the same URL as edm:isShownBy. ... This must be an image, even if it is for a sound object.
[[https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EF/pages/2106032160/ore+Aggregation#edm%3Aobject][https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EF/pages/2106032160/ore+Aggregation#edm%3Aobject]]

[2] Copyright metadata needs to be provided for every digital object submitted to Europeana and has to be mapped either to            
edm:rights ... For additional copyright information dc:rights may be used.                                                            
[[https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EF/pages/1503756289/Providing+copyright+metadata+to+Europeana#Available-values][https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EF/pages/1503756289/Providing+copyright+metadata+to+Europeana#Available-values]]
Ideally [dc:rights] should be applied to the edm:WebResource or the edm:ProvidedCHO. [[https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EF/pages/2106032160/ore+Aggregation#dc%3Arights][https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EF/pages/2106032160/ore+Aggregation#dc%3Arights]]

** edm:ProvidedCHO
The following are mandatory Europeana elements for the edm:ProvidedCHO. For local usage see also [[https://github.com/uchicago-library/UChicagoNode/wiki/Required-Elements][Required Elements]], which should be in agreement with what is stated here.

+ Either /dc:description/ or /dc:title/ or both.

+ One or more the following: /dc:subject/, /_dc:type_/, /dc:coverage/, /dcterms:spatial/, /dcterms:temporal/. [[https://europeana.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EF/pages/2106294284/edm+ProvidedCHO#dc%3Asubject]["... if more than one of these properties is available, please provide them all."]]

Local usage requires  _dc:type_. Values should be drawn from the [[https://www.dublincore.org/specifications/dublin-core/dcmi-terms/\#section-7][DCMI Type   Vocabulary]]. These are Collection, Dataset, Event, Image, InteractiveResource, MovingImage, PhysicalObject, Service, Software, Sound, StillImage, Text.  ``Note that digital representations of, or surrogates for, [PhysicalObject] should use Image, Text or one of the other types.''   

+ /dc:language/ for TEXT objects. It is strongly recommended for other   object types if there is a language aspect. Language codes   conforming to ISO 639 are used as values.

+ *edm:type* must occur and must use one of the following values (in   upper case): TEXT, IMAGE, SOUND, VIDEO or 3D. Map DCMI types to EDM   types as follows: 

: Image : IMAGE
: MovingImage : VIDEO
: Sound : SOUND
: StillImage : IMAGE
: Text : TEXT

In addition to what is specified above, the following is also required by local usage for the /edm:ProvidedCHO/.

+ _dc:identifier_. String-literal values for locally-created ARK identifiers are used, e.g.,
  "https://ark.lib.uchicago.edu/ark:61001/z9m865s34c01". 

+ _uchicago:identifier_. String-literal values assigned by the Digitization Unit are used, e.g., "G4104-C6-1933-U5-a".

For the following, see ``DCMI Kernel Metadata Community: Kernel Metadata and Electronic Resource Citations (ERCs)'', Section 3, Kernel
Stories. ([[https://www.dublincore.org/groups/kernel/spec/#anchor3][https://www.dublincore.org/groups/kernel/spec/#anchor3]]) They will support responses to queries about the metadata when the appropriate syntax is provided to an ARK resolver: ``ARK resolvers must support the `?info' inflection for requesting metadata.'' ([[https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-kunze-ark-28#section-1.2][https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-kunze-ark-28#section-1.2]]) See further in that document for the ?info inflection and the use of Electronic Resource Citations [ERCs].)

+ _erc:who_ The value is drawn from dc(terms):creator,   dc(terms):contributor, or dc(terms):publisher, in that order. If   none of those have values, then use erc:who ``(:unkn) unknown''.

+ _erc:what_ The value is drawn from dc:title or   dc:description, in that order. 

+ _erc:when_ String-literal values conforming to ISO 8601 or the   [[https://www.loc.gov/standards/datetime/][Extended Date/Time Format Specification (EDTF)]] are used in that order. If a date is not supplied, then use erc:when ``(:unkn)   unknown''.

+ _erc:where_ The value is drawn from dc:identifier, which must be present.

Any values which cannot be assigned should be drawn from ``DCMI Kernel Metadata Community: Kernel Metadata and Electronic Resource Citations
(ERCs)'', [[https://www.dublincore.org/groups/kernel/spec/#anchor16][Section 9.3, Special Kernel Standardized Value Codes]]. 

The following is an example of an edm:ProvidedCHO. This example does not include any elements specific to a particular digital collection
which may also be included in the edm:ProvidedCHO, for example, from BIBFRAME, VRA Core, etc. It includes only those elements discussed in this section.

#+BEGIN_SRC
<b20x2w73r321>                                                                                                                        
dc:contributor "Hanks, William F." , "Unnamed contributor (male)" ;                                                                   
dc:date "1979" ;                                                                                                                      
dc:description "Contents: \"History of Cooperativa\"" ;                                                                               
dc:language "spa" , "yua";                                                                                                            
dc:title "Yucatec Maya field recordings (Hanks, 1979-1987) Yucatán Maya" ;                                                            
dc:identifier "https://ark.lib.uchicago.edu/ark:61001/b20x2w73r321" ;                                                                 
dc:rights "https://rightsstatements.org/vocab/NoC-US/1.0/" ;                                                                          
dcterms:spatial "7005600" ;                                                                                                           
dc:type "Sound";
edm:type "SOUND" ;  
uchicago:identifier "G4104-C6-1933-U5-a";                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        
erc:who "Hanks, William F., interviewer; Unnamed contributor (male), consultant" ;                                                    
erc:what "Yucatec Maya field recordings (Hanks, 1979-1987) Yucatán Maya" ;                                                            
erc:when "1979" ;                                                                                                                     
erc:where "https://ark.lib.uchicago.edu/ark:61001/b20x2w73r321" ;                                                                     
a edm:ProvidedCHO . 
#+END_SRC

** ore:Proxy

The following are required for an ore:Proxy, which is optional; it is used only if one is associating a file of original descriptive
metadata, e.g., MARCXML or Dublin Core, with the aggregation. The requirements are indicated by example.

#+BEGIN_SRC
<b9m865s34c01/file.dc.xml>
dc:format "application/xml" ;
ore:proxyFor <b2nw3wm8552h> ;
ore:proxyIn <b2nw3wm8552h/aggregation> ;
a ore:Proxy .
#+END_SRC

Note that when an ore:ResourceMap is being created, the values of dcterms:created and dcterms:modified are the same.

** edm:WebResource

The following are required for an edm:WebResource. The requirements are indicated by example.

#+BEGIN_SRC
<b20x2w73r321/file.wav>                                                                                                               
ebucore:hasMimeType "audio/x-wav" ;                                                                                                   
dcterms:identifier "https://ark.lib.uchicago.edu/ark:61001/b20x2w73r321/file.wav" ;                                                   
premis:fixity [                                                                                                                       
  rdf:type <https://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/preservation/cryptographicHashFunctions/sha512> ;                                            
  rdf:value "10b1a2959f2229ab52e3873651c1d99036caa1e5d641e0bf257"] ;                                                                  
premis:originalName "FieldRecording1996-2.wav" ;                                                                                      
premis:size 44694436 ;                                                                                                                
a edm:WebResource . 
#+END_SRC

** rdfs:Resource

If rdfs:Resource is used, the following indicates its format. The example is for OCR data for a page object in Campus Publications.

#+BEGIN_SRC
<b2nw3wm8552h/00000001/file.xml>
dc:format "application/xml" ;
a rdfs:Resource . # This is the default type. 
#+END_SRC

